  "body": "## What changed\n\n- `cargo xtask gate light` is a new gate tier. It runs the light twins of the heavy tests in release.\n- The plan is one release build of the crates that hold a twin. Then it has one step for each test target with a twin (`motion light: lib`).\n- A light twin is found from the source. Its ignore reason starts with `light lane:`. Its name is `<full test>_light`.\n- The planner refuses a twin by name when its file has no `#[ignore]`d full test. A twin cannot take the place of its full test.\n- The first twin is `the_slot_keeps_its_verdict_under_sub_micron_perturbations_light` in `crates/motion/src/machining2d/adaptive/tests.rs`. It plans the slot 2 times. The full sweep keeps its 20 rows and does not change.\n- A red light run prints a note for the PR. The note names each red step and the command of its full heavy step: `cargo xtask gate release --only \"motion heavy: lib\"`.\n- AGENTS.md has two new named rules: **The light lane** (\"Testing\") and **Local full rerun** (\"Commits and Releases\").\n- `docs/decisions/2569-light-heavy-tier.md` records the choices.\n\n## Cause\n\n- A heavy test was skipped for each patch or run in full at the cut. There was no tier between the two.\n- A red heavy test stayed unseen until the cut gate. A red cut gate costs about 53 minutes.\n\n## Tests\n\nPins, all in `xtask/src/light_tests.rs`:\n\n- `gate_light_is_a_tier_of_its_own`\n- `light_plan_is_one_release_build_then_one_step_for_each_target_with_a_twin`\n- `the_slot_sweep_keeps_its_full_test_and_has_a_light_twin`\n- `a_light_twin_needs_its_name_and_its_full_test_next_to_it`\n- `a_red_light_run_names_the_full_heavy_rerun_of_each_red_step`\n- `the_law_names_the_light_lane_and_the_local_full_rerun`\n\nRed before the change: yes. On unchanged code the pins do not compile (`unresolved import crate::light`). This is a new tier, thus there is no earlier behaviour to fail an assert.\n\nMutations:\n\n- The refusal of a twin without its full test was removed: `a_light_twin_needs_its_name_and_its_full_test_next_to_it` was red. Restored: green.\n- The `light` tier was removed from `parse_gate`: `gate_light_is_a_tier_of_its_own` was red. Restored: green.\n- The `light:` to `heavy:` mapping of the note was removed: `a_red_light_run_names_the_full_heavy_rerun_of_each_red_step` was red. Restored: green.\n- A false assert was added to the twin: `cargo xtask gate light` was red (exit code 1) and printed the note with `cargo xtask gate release --only \"motion heavy: lib\"`. Restored: green.\n\nReadings of the real run (`cargo xtask gate light`, Linux, 6 jobs):\n\n- First release build of `camcraft-motion`: 412 s. A warm build after one test edit: 49 s.\n- `motion light: lib`: 18 s. It ran 1 test, and the test passed.\n\nGate:\n\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main`: green, in two runs. The plan has 9 steps.\n  - Run 1 passed steps 1 to 6: `motion build`, `motion suites: lib` (451 passed, 790 s), `adaptive_band`, `adaptive_hsm`, `adaptive_orbit_seam`, `pocket3d_hsm`. The harness stopped the run at its time limit during step 7. No step was red.\n  - Run 2 passed the other 3 steps with `--only`: `motion suites: rest_adaptive` (243 s), `motion suites: shape_masks`, `xtask unit tests` (112 s).\n- `cargo clippy -p xtask -p camcraft-motion --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n\n## Goldens moved\n\nNone.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- The full heavy sweep (`the_slot_keeps_its_verdict_under_sub_micron_perturbations`) was not run. This PR does not change it.\n- `cargo xtask gate release` was not run. Its heavy steps run each ignored test, thus they run the twin too (about 18 s more).\n- No run on Windows or macOS.\n- The light tier is not wired into `/review-prs`, `/merge-ready` or `pr-test.yml`. Issue #2568 owns when the heavy tests of a PR run.\n\n## Owed: the skill text\n\nThe issue asks that the cut skill names the local full rerun step. This PR does not change `.claude/skills/`. The worker session could not write there: the harness refused each edit of `.claude/skills/gate/SKILL.md` and `.claude/skills/release-cut/SKILL.md`. The rules are in AGENTS.md in this PR. A comment on this PR has the text for the two skill files. A session with that permission can push it to this branch. For this reason the PR has `Refs #2569` and not `Fixes #2569`.\n\n## Overlaps\n\nNone. No open PR changes `xtask/src/`, `AGENTS.md` or `crates/motion/src/machining2d/adaptive/tests.rs`. PR #2643 and PR #2606 change other files in `xtask/tests/`.\n\nProcess change: yes\n\nEffort: high\n\nChangelog: none\n\nRefs #2569\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
